Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Maybe, in definition of puncture, turn it into u slicing \
immediately so everything is using u slicing.\n\nCurrently, the corrector \
tensors are computed separately for the right and left side to the particle\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s radius. One should be able to combine them into a single \
NDSolve. Even if the stress energy is discontinuous, Mathematica has way to \
handle this; ",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["see here for more details.",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/tutorial/NDSolveWhenEvents.\
html#1688891301"], None},
  ButtonNote->
   "https://reference.wolfram.com/language/tutorial/NDSolveWhenEvents.html#\
1688891301"],
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 StyleBox["\n\nresidual reconstructed metric is really only defined inside \
the worldtube.",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8776836181786833`*^9, 3.877683725913144*^9}, {
   3.877684259490835*^9, 3.8776843694104548`*^9}, {3.879845847011992*^9, 
