  3.872760381089493*^9, 3.872760381823805*^9}, {3.8776835621470947`*^9, 
  3.877683577737121*^9}, {3.877684171346981*^9, 3.8776841907177353`*^9}, {
  3.8780335053855658`*^9, 
  3.8780335059539127`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"293aed75-f589-4e11-9e82-\
906a224b137a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The delta function of the stress-energy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["T", "ab"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e1315914-6550-495c-b9a9-058f2319f1b0"],
 " cancels with those produced by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalE]h", "p"], ")"}], "ab"], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"5ccd9a11-cdcc-4f29-a05c-3681e314b853"],
 ".\nWe can therefore treat ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalE]h", "p"], ")"}], "ab"], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"b07ed75a-8557-4400-936d-277230c51491"],
 " as an ordinary function. The distributional pieces we do need to take into \
account are those from derivatives of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalTheta]", "M"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4f004eb2-38f1-486a-95cd-c71f18842f30"],
 "(r) by setting ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["h", "p"], " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["h", "p"], " ", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalTheta]", "M"], "(", "r", ")"}]}]}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"5b2feae0-481d-43d2-82e8-b819f82891f1"],
 " before differentiating."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8736295956284113`*^9, 3.873629795199284*^9}, 
   3.87363000657018*^9, {3.8931525928217993`*^9, 
   3.893152601262023*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cb151534-ee9d-4a24-909f-\
9e3cc6f6b603"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["This section ",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 StyleBox["needs",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True},
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 StyleBox[" to be evaluated before setting numerical quantities!!!!",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8738208697284403`*^9, 3.8738208839451303`*^9}, {
  3.876828740682845*^9, 3.876828742074121*^9}, {3.877164222515888*^9, 
  3.877164223874194*^9}, {3.8771642586669416`*^9, 
  3.877164260073145*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5f942477-6b9a-468f-87d7-\
b6b6460758c8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"Clear", "[", "\[CapitalTheta]M", "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalTheta]M", "[", "r_", "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"HeavisideTheta", "[", 
     RowBox[{"r", "-", "rmin"}], "]"}], "-", 
    RowBox[{"HeavisideTheta", "[", 
     RowBox[{"r", "-", "rmax"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.873196679393406*^9, 3.873196689030409*^9}, {
  3.887263683039312*^9, 3.887263685334435*^9}, {3.892875070071763*^9, 
  3.892875074092032*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[147]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3be1f08b-6d15-4c48-b950-ce6b48f8eb22"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["General expression", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.872757918910462*^9, 3.87275792337864*^9}, {
   3.872760381089493*^9, 3.872760381823805*^9}, {3.873629352662136*^9, 
   3.8736293554755774`*^9}, {3.893777961225232*^9, 3.893777964436627*^9}, 
   3.893778000959651*^9},ExpressionUUID->"821935f1-2d6f-43d2-a598-\
15f30b25b74f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The below is taken from Andrew\[CloseCurlyQuote]s notebook. The spherical \
harmonics can be factored out. Expressed in Kinnersley tetrad, where blue \
indices are tetrad indices (1,2,3,4) = (l,n,m,mb). As it assumes mostly \
positive convention, need to add a minus sign. For this to make sense, also \
need the input to be in mostly negative convention!\nAssuming a Fourier \
series expansion in t.\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Mu]", "n", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "44b5acdc-d2da-4d2d-91ed-4ed391a738f7"],
 " := ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"l", "+", "n"}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"l", "-", "n", "+", "1"}], ")"}]}]], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"fa6be87d-41da-47ad-9a2a-209d51f14999"],
 ". ,1 in green means derivative wrt to radius R (usual Schwarzschild \
coordinates).\nThe list of dG is  {ll,ln,lm,lmb,nn,nm,nmb,mm,mmb,mbmb}. \
\[Omega]1 = m \[CapitalOmega].\nThe metric has been expanded in frequency of \
exp(-i\[Omega]t). To use null tetrad representation, we want \
exp(-i\[Omega]u), where u=t-r*."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8736288666753693`*^9, 3.873628956575698*^9}, {
  3.873628988808755*^9, 3.8736291143472633`*^9}, {3.873643943616372*^9, 
  3.873643987685309*^9}, {3.87379059401873*^9, 3.873790597740472*^9}, {
  3.878535280790183*^9, 3.878535304612356*^9}, {3.883804653023693*^9, 
  3.883804725704637*^9}, {3.888392429279871*^9, 3.888392430254093*^9}, {
  3.898690383320201*^9, 
  3.898690459167596*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"21924a65-eb87-4164-85ba-\
5cd5750da3aa"],

