Cell["\<\
The puncture is given in trace reversed form!
If you want to change this, then need to invert BLS indices 3 and 6, both for \
the below code, and do something about the data in the file h0-deriv4.m!!

Also, the puncture hPLorentz computed below via exact integration of the \
\[Beta] integrals are in (-,+,+,+) convention.
As a result, should only use the functions defined in the next section \
instead, called hP.\
\>", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,
