14cb2d07f996"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This calculation of the corrector tensors is exact, but relies on a \
power-series expansion of the puncture.\nFundamentally, this was given up in \
favor of a numerical approach, because the resulting corrector tensors\
\[CloseCurlyQuote] l modes do not converge away from the particle (which is \
needed for second order).\n\nIn order to run this section, you actually do \
not need the coefficient of the power series expansion, as the result is \
written in terms of them.\nYou do however need the expression of the stress \
energy in terms of the metric. The section \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Rules\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] will then replace the metric perturbation as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"~", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"r", "-", 
        SubscriptBox["r", "0"]}], ")"}]}], ")"}], "aExp"], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"f3abe77e-4835-4e77-8abd-0a81e5788c34"],
 ", and then compute the integrals exactly.\nNote that in general, there are \
three different sources of contributions: distributional contrbutions (at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["r", "min"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b4250ded-3cac-41d0-a7ca-193fd492b117"],
 "), pieces ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"~", "\[CapitalDelta]r"}], ")"}], "n"], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"1c87f972-a488-4724-bb9d-4c357e46bbb7"],
 " and pieces ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"|", "\[CapitalDelta]r", "|", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]r", 
     RowBox[{"n", "-", "1"}]]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b28db838-9705-4d93-8350-470ac41483a6"],
 ", see \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Theory\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] section for \
more details.\n\nThe aExp then need to be run from 0 to whatever order you \
want. If you want to use these results to then compute the coefficients of \
\[CapitalXi], you only need to go to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"aExp", "=", "1"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "25ef266f-4ccb-4312-928b-0c41e918496b"],
 ", as higher order terms where empirically checked to not contribute (up to \
aExp=4)."
}], "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.893583519926118*^9, 3.8935838030597067`*^9}, {
  3.89358384501803*^9, 
  3.8935839192901163`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4d777c37-b167-466c-aef8-\
3f95fdf0a5a4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"aExp", "=", "0"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 Evaluatable->False,
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
